# Emulators this console installs from Flathub, pinned to exact revisions.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# Two emulators cannot be libretro cores and come from Flathub: xemu and Eden
# are standalone applications with their own windows and renderers. RPCS3 was
# the third until 2026-09-28; it is now the RPCS3 team's own build, in /usr,
# because its Flatpak shows a warning box on every start. See
# build_files/install-rpcs3.sh.
#
# They are NOT baked into the image, and that is not a limitation we are working
# around — it is what bootc requires. A flatpak installs into /var, and bootc
# unpacks /var from the container image ONLY on the initial install: "subsequent
# changes to /var in a container image are not automatically applied". Baked in,
# an emulator would land once on a fresh machine and then never move again, and
# would do nothing at all on a machine that already exists. It would look like
# it worked. See docs/PROJECT.md, open question 21.
#
# So they are installed on first boot, and this file is how the image says which
# revision. Same model as the libretro cores in cores/build-core.sh: an exact
# commit, in the image, that moves only when someone edits it here.
#
# THE RUNTIME IS PINNED TOO, and that is the point rather than a detail. A
# flatpak sits on a shared runtime carrying its Qt, graphics and audio
# libraries. Pinning only the app would mean two machines installing the SAME
# CabinetOS image a month apart get different libraries underneath the same
# emulator — same image version, different behaviour, and a bug report that
# depends on the date somebody installed. Pinning both means the image version
# alone says what is on the machine.
#
# HOW TO MOVE A VERSION
#
#   flatpak remote-info --system flathub <app>           # current commit
#   flatpak remote-info --system --log flathub <app>     # earlier commits
#
# Edit the commit here, in its own commit, and say why in the message. Nothing
# else moves it: the flatpak auto-update timers are masked by strip-desktop.sh.
#
# FORMAT — four fields, whitespace separated. Blank lines and lines starting
# with # are ignored. Nothing may follow the fields, not even a comment: the
# console would read it into the commit, and the build refuses it.
#
#   <kind>    app or runtime
#   <ref>     the flatpak ref, without the arch
#   <branch>  the branch
#   <commit>  the exact revision to hold
#
# A runtime must be listed before the apps that use it, so it is installed at
# the right revision rather than pulled in as a dependency at whatever is
# current. Commits below were read off Flathub on 2026-09-18.

# --- runtimes -------------------------------------------------------------

runtime  org.freedesktop.Platform  25.08  d27f7a6a974e40b061070bec1be9e1b52a7a6872b271e6a45c2c34a48bf6fedf
runtime  org.kde.Platform          6.11   4da4797cdce707e1db7bc25720ac5e1f56818c087621f3737ea5482b0ed53c18

# --- emulators ------------------------------------------------------------

# Original Xbox, played since #172 (docs/PROJECT.md, open question 33). Its
# blank drive and the EEPROM are in the image; see install-xemu-drive.sh.
app  app.xemu.xemu      stable  2f8b8889edcf69fb2ba2a8691371a7bb49febeba360e9c87555379c50ba946e9

# Nintendo Switch.
app  dev.eden_emu.eden  stable  88af3f795612d92099a71e4ed63d8219ee04088dcd9cfb5776ae595940425091
